From: TxCsOffc <243226414+TxCsOffc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: opt-in lazy AFP, no FPCR writes on calls between x64 and ARM64EC code

Each call between x64 and ARM64EC code wrote FPCR twice: ExitFunctionEC cleared AH and NEP on the way out and the
JIT set them again on the way in, and so did every call into FEX's helpers. An FPCR write stalls Apple cores; in
saved Forza Horizon 6 profiles the write in ExitFunctionEC was FEX's hottest instruction, about 19% of a hot thread.

HB_FEX_LAZY_AFP=1 makes the JIT use NEP but not AH: x86 MIN/MAX and RCP/RSQRT are emulated as on hosts without AFP,
and RPRES is not used, since it needs AH. Scalar min/max explicitly insert the FCSEL result to preserve x86's upper
lanes. tests/x64-fidelity/scalarminmax.c checks all 128 destination bits. ExitFunctionEC leaves NEP set and clears
only the trap enables, and
only when one is armed, so neither native calls nor helper calls write FPCR. Without the switch, the exit mask is
the three old ones in one load, and the JIT is unchanged, so everyone pays one load per exit.

Under the switch the program sees these differences:

- With AH clear, FPCR.FZ flushes denormal inputs as well as outputs, so a program that sets MXCSR.FTZ without DAZ
  also gets DAZ. x87test's mxcsr.ftz.flags shows the related one: no PE after a flushed underflow.
- The default NaN is positive, where x86's indefinite NaN is negative.
- NEP stays set in native code. That includes macOS code, since Wine's unix call dispatcher does not touch FPCR, not
  only ARM64EC code. With NEP set, a scalar SIMD&FP instruction keeps the upper lanes of its destination instead of
  zeroing them, and LLVM assumes they are zeroed, so compiled code that relies on that, in Wine, the CRT or a macOS
  library, can compute different results. Wine's CRT math gave bit-identical results over 10,610 calls with NEP set,
  but that does not cover other native code. Leaving AH set the same way did change the CRT's results (sinh(-1)
  came out positive), which is why the switch drops AH rather than keeping it.
- FIZ, set from MXCSR.DAZ, stays set while FEX's own helpers run.

On an M5 Max, macOS 27.2 (2026-11-17): a native call 24.0 to 4.3 ns, QueryPerformanceCounter 40 to 20 ns, scalar SSE
unchanged, SSE MIN/MAX 1.80 to 2.27 ns. The x64 fidelity programs give the same results except x87test's
mxcsr.ftz.flags. Forza Horizon 6 played normally with it. Off unless HB_FEX_LAZY_AFP=1 is set.

Built for arm64ec on FEX 2610 plus 0001 to 0034.
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
index 8986ec4cf00ef30eccc11195d965941fbbf3944d..cde5cefbe8fff2f31a14d0f40e6a9cfc429b3e5e 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
@@ -650,9 +650,13 @@ void Arm64Emitter::FillSpecialRegs(ARMEmitter::Register TmpReg, ARMEmitter::Regi
     //
     // Additional interesting AFP bits:
     // FIZ(0): Flush Inputs to Zero
-    orr(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg,
-        (1U << 2) |   // NEP
-          (1U << 1)); // AH
+    if (FEXCore::Context::HbLazyAFP) {
+      orr(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg, 1U << 2); // NEP only (Highball HB_FEX_LAZY_AFP)
+    } else {
+      orr(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg,
+          (1U << 2) |   // NEP
+            (1U << 1)); // AH
+    }
 
     if (Options.SetFIZ) {
       // Insert MXCSR.DAZ in to FIZ
@@ -706,7 +710,18 @@ void Arm64Emitter::FillSpecialRegs(ARMEmitter::Register TmpReg, ARMEmitter::Regi
 
 void Arm64Emitter::SpillStaticRegs(ARMEmitter::Register TmpReg, SpillStaticRegOptions Options) {
 #ifndef VIXL_SIMULATOR
-  if (EmitterCTX->HostFeatures.SupportsAFP) {
+  if (EmitterCTX->HostFeatures.SupportsAFP && FEXCore::Context::HbLazyAFP) {
+    // Highball HB_FEX_LAZY_AFP: keep NEP and FIZ for FEX's helpers (AH is never set); clear the trap enables only when one is armed
+    ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel NoTraps;
+    mrs(TmpReg, ARMEmitter::SystemRegister::FPCR);
+    and_(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg, 0xff00);
+    (void)cbz(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, &NoTraps);
+    mrs(TmpReg, ARMEmitter::SystemRegister::FPCR);
+    bic(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg, 0x1f00);
+    bic(ARMEmitter::Size::i64Bit, TmpReg, TmpReg, 0x8000);
+    msr(ARMEmitter::SystemRegister::FPCR, TmpReg);
+    (void)Bind(&NoTraps);
+  } else if (EmitterCTX->HostFeatures.SupportsAFP) {
     // Disable AFP features when spilling registers.
     //
     // Disable FPCR.NEP and FPCR.AH and FPCR.FIZ
